 "_luma": "WCAG relative luminance. mean = average over the cell; hot = FRACTION of samples too bright for cream. Cream product names are drawn straight onto the artwork with no reading card behind them, so a name may only sit where the artwork stays DARK enough for cream to hold contrast. Cream #FFF8EF is L=0.947, so contrast against a cell is (0.997)/(L+0.05); AA for large text is 3.0, which means L must stay under ~0.283. peak is what actually matters \u2014 a cell averaging dark because it is half purple and half cream drip would still swallow the glyphs crossing it. A FRACTION rather than the peak, because one star lands a single bright sample in an otherwise-purple cell and vetoing that cell would forbid most of the frame for no legibility gain.",
